{"id": "3a9f793e-786a-4d6b-b91d-da4b15883746", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a broad survey task across accounts/regions, not a debugging investigation, so it's better suited for a background sub-agent to assess AgentCore runtimes and gateways rather than asking clarifying questions first. There's no dedicated skill for AgentCore specifically, though SageMaker-related ones might be relevant.

I'll have the sub-agent check associated accounts too, keeping everything read-only, and draft a brief plan message before launching it.

"}]}

{"id": "6c5cd3ec-3d18-4ea6-8dc2-4c3ec3e76a61", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your Bedrock AgentCore runtimes and gateways for network (VPC) configuration and encryption settings, across the accounts and regions this space can access. It's a read-only survey, so I'm running it in the background.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_MHVWRiateVbDYG70TNSpDj", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "agentcore-security-assessment", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security assessment of Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtimes and Gateways, focused on VPC/network isolation and encryption. Produce severity-rated findings (High/Medium/Low/Info) with resource identifiers.",
  "context": "The user asked: 'Assess our Bedrock AgentCore runtimes and gateways for VPC and encryption security.' Agent space account is 012345678901_1 (us-east-1). Use list_associations to find other associated AWS accounts and cover them too. Check every region where AgentCore is available (start with us-east-1, us-west-2, eu-central-1, ap-southeast-2, ap-southeast-1, ap-northeast-1, eu-west-1 and any others where resources are found). Use the boto3 'bedrock-agentcore-control' client (list_agent_runtimes, get_agent_runtime, list_gateways, get_gateway, list_gateway_targets, get_gateway_target, and where useful list_agent_runtime_endpoints, list_memories, list_workload_identities, list_api_key_credential_providers/oauth2 providers). Only use read-only calls. If an API name is unavailable in the installed boto3 version, use verify_aws_claim to confirm the correct operation or fields.",
  "resources": ["All AgentCore agent runtimes, runtime endpoints, gateways, and gateway targets in accessible accounts/regions"],
  "criteria": "Runtimes: networkConfiguration.networkMode (PUBLIC vs VPC); if VPC, subnets/security groups and whether SGs are overly permissive (0.0.0.0/0 ingress/egress on broad ports); protocolConfiguration; authorizerConfiguration (IAM SigV4 vs custom JWT, allowed audiences/clients); execution role broadness (check attached/inline policies for wildcard actions/resources, read-only); environment variables that look like secrets; ECR/container source; lifecycle configuration. Gateways: authorizerType (NONE/AWS_IAM/CUSTOM_JWT), kmsKeyArn (customer-managed key vs service-owned), protocol config, exceptionLevel/debug exposure, target types and credential provider configs (API key/OAuth/IAM), whether targets are reachable only publicly. Also check for VPC endpoints (com.amazonaws.<region>.bedrock-agentcore and bedrock-agentcore.gateway) in the VPCs used, and whether the KMS keys used have rotation enabled and a sane key policy (read-only describe/get calls). Memory resources: encryptionKeyArn. Summarize: inventory counts per account/region, a findings table sorted by severity, and recommended remediations. If nothing is found in a region/account, state that explicitly. Keep the report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Assess AgentCore runtimes and gateways for VPC and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

